course: dictionary
lesson: 7296
title: A false friend: piscine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look like English words but mean something else. These are called false friends. «Piscine» is one of them. In English it is a rare, formal word, and in French it is a common everyday word.
explain: In English, piscine means to do with fish or like a fish. A «piscine smell» is a fishy smell. It is a science word, so you might find it in a book about sea creatures.
explain: In French, «une piscine» means a swimming pool. It sounds like «pee-SEEN», and it is a French word, not an English one. If the text is in French, piscine means a pool.
explain: Use the context to decide. Fish, science and smells point to the English meaning. French words around it, such as «la» or «à», point to the French meaning.
fact: Piscine (English, formal) means to do with fish or like a fish.
fact: «Une piscine» (French) means a swimming pool.
fact: A false friend is a word that looks or sounds like a word you know, but means something different.
fact: «Tu vas où ?» means "Where are you going?", «À la piscine !» means "To the swimming pool!", and «Moi aussi !» means "Me too!"
fact: French joins à and le into au, so you say «au parc», but «à la piscine» and «à l'école» stay apart.
exercise: A scientist writes about a piscine shape in a fish. What does piscine mean here? | A very large cloud | A sort of bird | A swimming pool | *To do with fish or like a fish
exercise: In French class, Ella reads «Tu vas où ?» and «À la piscine !». What does «la piscine» mean? | A park | A fish | *A swimming pool | A school
exercise: Maya says piscine means a swimming pool, so she must be talking about English. What is wrong with her idea? | Piscine is a type of bird | Nothing is wrong, it means a pool in English | It is a French word for a fish | *That is the French meaning, so she must check whether the text is in French
test: In a French book, «une piscine» means: | A bird's nest | A cold lake | *A swimming pool | A fish tank
test: In an English science book, piscine means: | A swimming pool | *Like a fish | Made of glass | Very loud
exam: Which is the correct English meaning of piscine, and which is the French meaning of «une piscine»? | A swimming pool; like a fish | Like a bird; a park | *Like a fish; a swimming pool | Like a cloud; a school
